<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<hr />
<p>Would it be feasible to simply cut &quot;SCP-3322-&quot; when discussing residents, and rearrange what's left to place their location over their individual designations (For ease of reference, I figure it'd flow easier to know immediately which town they belonged to rather than which resident they are of the town.)?</p>
<p>For the agents, maybe a symbol could be used to further differentiate them from residents? Also, unless the names are super important, I'd consider cutting them; see how that affects readability.</p>
<p>So:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3322-1568-A (Mr O. Vidal), wielding a hunting rifle, shoots and kills his wife, SCP-3322-1569-A (Mrs M. Vidal), during a heated argument. SCP-3322-0-B (Agent B. Ganbold) is informed of these events 2 hours later by SCP-3322-0-A (Agent G. Martin) and he investigates the residence of SCP-3322-1568-B (Mr A. Gantulga) and SCP-3322-1569-B (Ms O. Bayarmaa).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Would look like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A-1568, wielding a hunting rifle, shoots and kills his wife, A-1569, during a heated argument. Ω-B is informed of these events 2 hours later by Ω-A and he investigates the residence of B-1568 and B-1569.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p>This:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3322-0-A (Agent E. Santos) and B (Agent V. Navalny) are discovered to have been involved in an intimate relationship with SCP-3322-491-A (Ms C. Herrera) and B (Ms O. Erdenchimeg) for the previous 3 months.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Would look like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Ω-A and Ω-B are discovered to have been involved in an intimate relationship with A-491 and B-491 for the previous 3 months.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>(Hell, you could also call the personnel: Operative-B and Operative-A)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Operative-A and Operative-B are discovered to have been involved in an intimate relationship with A-491 and B-491 for the previous 3 months.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p>This:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3322-A. SCP-3322-2201-A and SCP-3322-3977-A visible in foreground.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Would appear as:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3322-A. A-2201 and A-3977 visible in foreground.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p>In cases where name matters, simple rewording should provide sufficient context:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On 1/03/1995, SCP-3322-1-B (Mayor C. Batu) announces he will use his personal funds to construct a house for the use of SCP-3322-0-B (Agent B. Ganbold)</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>On 1/03/1995, the mayor of SCP-3322-B announces he will use his personal funds to construct a house for the use of Ω-B.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p>Hell, maybe you can drop the designations altogether in some places and go with names instead:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Mr O. Vidal, wielding a hunting rifle, shoots and kills his wife during a heated argument. Agent B. Ganbold is informed of these events 2 hours later by Agent G. Martin and he investigates the residence of the corresponding couple in Buyant.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Agents E. Santos and V. Navalny are each discovered to have been involved in an intimate relationship with corresponding civilians for the previous 3 months.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>On 1/03/1995, the mayor of Buyant announces he will use his personal funds to construct a house for the use of Operative B.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p>Not perfect, but you could stand to play around with it until you find something workable.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

